ence versus absence was claimed to be more negative, but the signed estimate is -0.829 with interval -0.891 to -0.767, so the raw effect is approximately +0.829. The original negative claim H31 is rejected as registered, but the magnitude and precision suggest that a reversed positive claim should be investigated. I registered a reversed feature_010 claim with positive direction, parent H31, initially unresolved, because the discovered raw association is very large and not an artifact of a tiny cell. Overall, most screens are null or implausibly small relative to the 0.15 threshold. The strongest valid directional candidate is H17; the strongest large association is the opposite-direction feature_010 effect. All conclusions remain dataset-specific unadjusted associations, not causal claims, and the large feature_010 association warrants caution about coding or unmeasured structure even though its statistical signal is strong. Multiplicity remains a concern because many opaque nominal and binary predictors are being screened, so borderline or post hoc effects should not be accepted without adequate precision or independent confirmation.",
