  "narrative": "No independent validation was requested because the voluntary validation quota is exhausted (remaining_new_requests=0). I audited the newly delivered discovery evidence using the pre-specified absolute threshold of 0.15 composite dependency-score units, with attention to interval uncertainty, cell sizes, post hoc multiple comparisons, sparse subgroup structure, and the fact that feature_038 and feature_018 are opaque standardized assays rather than known biological modifiers. For feature_063, the main context tests are informative. H228 (feature_038>=0.75) gives signed +0.556 [0.356,0.756] in the claimed negative direction (R210), with exposed/comparator cells 62/397. The entire interval exceeds the threshold, so I accept it as a dataset-specific association: in this supplied dataset, feature_063=1 is associated with a lower outcome_001 more strongly in high feature_038 context. H229 (feature_018<=-0.75) gives signed +0.348 [0.165,0.530] (R211), cells 67/378. Although the lower bound is close to threshold, it remains above it and the point estimate is substantial, consistent with the attenuation model: the negative feature_063 association is retained when feature_018 is low. H230 (feature_018>=0.75) gives signed -0.104 [-0.288,0.081] (R212); this is wrong direction relative to a negative claim and imprecise, so I reject the claim that feature_063 has a meaningful negative effect in high feature_018 context by itself. This supports attenuation rather than simple uniform effect rescaling. For clean all-major-tag-absent interactions, H232 (feature_063 by feature_038>=0.75, direction negative) gives signed +0.358 [0.179,0.538] (R214), with adequate cell counts overall. The entire interval exceeds threshold, so I accept that the feature_063 contrast is meaningfully more negative in high feature_038 among the clean-tag setting tested. H231 (feature_063 by feature_018>=0.75, direction positive) gives signed +0.299 [0.152,0.446] (R213), indicating attenuation of the negative feature_063 contrast at very high feature_018. I accept this cautiously because the lower bound only barely exceeds threshold and the extreme exposed cell is small; I defer the investigation rather than treating it as settled. The specificity tests for dominant tags are all unsupported: H233 feature_027 by feature_038 is wrong direction and imprecise (R215), H234 feature_027 by feature_018 is near null (R216), H235 feature_037 by feature_038 is below threshold (R217), H236 feature_037 by feature_018 is wrong direction/near null (R218), H237 feature_002 by feature_038 is below threshold (R219), and H238 feature_010 by feature_018 is below threshold despite a nominally positive point (R220). These rejections do not prove absence of moderate interactions, because several intervals are wide, but they argue against a broad interpretation in which high feature_038 or high feature_018 uniformly rescale the dominant feature_010, feature_002, feature_027, or feature_037 associations. The feature_017 screen H115 gives signed -0.057 [-0.185,0.071] (R221); I reject it. The reciprocal claim H116 is also unsupported on the same evidence, with a positive-direction point below threshold and an interval crossing threshold, so I close it as reject. I also close H215 as unresolved because its clean feature_018-by-feature_063 interaction did not exceed threshold and additional post hoc splitting is unlikely to resolve it. Overall, these new results sharpen the dataset-specific context model: feature_063 behaves as a negative association whose strength is gated upward by feature_038 and attenuated by feature_018, while the dominant tag associations are not broadly modified in the same way. All conclusions remain associations in this supplied dataset, not causal, mechanistic, biological, clinical, or generalizable claims.",
