  "narrative": "No assessments are due and no new independent-validation request is available, so this stage registers bounded within-dataset refinements aimed at the final open issue: whether the feature_063 context model is coherent and whether it is specific to the tested tag-absence context. The pre-specified scientific threshold remains 0.15 absolute composite dependency-score units, and any result with an interval crossing that threshold, an insufficient cell count, or a wrong-direction point estimate will be treated as unresolved or unsupported rather than proof of absence.\n\nThe first proposal tests the attenuation model outside the strongest feature_038 gate: in the clean all-major-tag-absent setting, where feature_063 has an accepted moderate negative association, the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast should remain meaningful and probably stronger when feature_018 is low. This is a direct refinement of H215, whose interaction contrast suggested feature_018 attenuation but whose lower interval did not fully clear threshold. If this low-feature_018 contrast exceeds threshold with adequate cells, it supports the idea that feature_018 modifies feature_063 association even without conditioning on high feature_038 and without relying on dominant-tag exclusion. A null or below-threshold result would limit the attenuation evidence to the stronger feature_038-gated or more extreme contrasts already observed.\n\nThe second proposal is the complementary clean high-feature_018 contrast. I expect attenuation, possibly below the threshold, but I register the negative claim with uncertain anticipated direction because the existing high-feature_018 contexts have sometimes retained a substantial negative association when feature_038 is also high. If this clean high-feature_018 main effect is well below threshold while the low-feature_018 contrast is above threshold, that pattern supports attenuation. If both remain meaningful, the context effect is weaker than a threshold-rescuing model suggests. If the high-feature_018 result is wrong direction, that would weaken the attenuation interpretation.\n\nThe third proposal asks whether high feature_038 is still necessary for a strong feature_063 negative association when feature_018 is low. It conditions on the same clean all-major-tag-absent context but requires both low feature_038 and low feature_018. The plausible alternative outcomes are: a threshold-supported negative result would mean low feature_018 can support the feature_063 signal without high feature_038, expanding the context model; a null or near-null result would preserve the more specific model in which high feature_038 is the key upward gate and feature_018 mainly attenuates within gated contexts. Because this is a conditional subgroup search, I will weight it cautiously if cells are small or interval lower bounds are near threshold.\n\nThe fourth proposal tests robustness in a less strict setting: all participants with high feature_038 and low feature_018, without excluding the dominant positive tags or the dominant negative tags. I expect a meaningful negative feature_063 contrast if the feature_038/feature_018 context model is not merely an artifact of the clean-tag restriction. This is a dataset-specific robustness check, not a claim that feature_038 and feature_018 cause, explain, or biologically define the feature_063 association. If this broad context exceeds threshold, it strengthens the practical compact model; if it is null or imprecise, the feature_063 context model should remain limited to the cleaner settings where it was most stable.\n\nAll four comparisons remain association-only conclusions in this supplied dataset. They do not establish causality, mechanism, clinical relevance, or generalizability. They do not change the established dominant-tag hierarchy (feature_010 and feature_002 positive; feature_027 and feature_037 negative), and they do not require the constructed binary research markers to be biologically meaningful."
}

