  "narrative": "No assessments are due, and no independent validation request can be made because the voluntary validation quota is exhausted. The scientific threshold remains 0.15 absolute composite dependency-score units, and any signed estimates and intervals will be interpreted directly without re-multiplying by the registered direction. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations only; they are not causal, biological, mechanistic, clinical, or generalizable claims.\n\nThe primary scientific need is still to resolve the feature_063 context model. The current compact model is that feature_063 is not a robust marginal negative tag, but a negative feature_063 association is enabled by high feature_038 and attenuated by high feature_018. The active untested clean refinement H250 is the most informative remaining test of whether the feature_038 gate remains threshold-supported when feature_018 is high after removing the dominant feature_010, feature_002, feature_027, and feature_037 composition channels. I keep H250 available and register complementary clean boundary tests rather than re-registering the same comparison.\n\nThe first new proposal refines the accepted broad low-feature_018 feature_038-gate test H244 by requiring absence of the four dominant tags. This asks whether the strong feature_063-by-feature_038 gate in the low-feature_018 context is intrinsic to the feature_063/feature_038 relationship rather than driven by correlated dominant tags. I anticipate a negative raw interaction, meaning the feature_063 contrast is more negative when feature_038 is high than when it is low among low feature_018. If threshold-supported, this confirms the gate in the clean low-feature_018 stratum. If it is near threshold or opposite, the accepted gate is less stable than currently believed once dominant tags are removed.\n\nThe second and third proposals complete a cleaner feature_038-by-feature_018 boundary map. The second tests a negative feature_063 main contrast in the clean low-feature_038/high-feature_018 context, and the third tests the same in the clean low-feature_038/low-feature_018 context. Existing clean high-feature_038 contexts are strong, especially high-feature_038/low-feature_018 and high-feature_038/high-feature_018. These new tests ask whether meaningful negative associations can occur without high feature_038. The anticipated raw contrasts are uncertain: low-feature_018 alone should not be sufficient without the feature_038 gate, while high feature_018 alone should not be sufficient and may even attenuate the association. Threshold-supported negative contrasts in either context would expand the context model; near-null contrasts would support the current interpretation that high feature_038 is required and high feature_018 is not sufficient.\n\nThe fourth proposal refines the broad low-feature_038 feature_063-by-feature_018 attenuation test H245 by removing dominant-tag composition. This is a specificity check for the feature_018 modifier. A threshold-supported positive raw interaction, meaning high feature_018 makes the feature_063 contrast less negative than low feature_018 among low feature_038, would indicate that feature_018 attenuation is not confined to the high-feature_038 gate. A near-null or below-threshold interaction would be compatible with the current model: feature_018 modification is most interpretable in feature_063 contexts where high feature_038 provides enough signal to detect attenuation.\n\nThe fifth proposal tests a feature_063-by-feature_044 interaction within the clean high-feature_038 gate. This is a deliberate specificity test against the established feature_018 modifier. The registered attenuation direction asks whether high feature_044 makes the negative feature_063 contrast less negative, as high feature_018 does. I expect little modification because feature_044 has no prior association or modifier evidence, so the anticipated raw interaction is near zero. A threshold-supported attenuation would broaden the context model beyond feature_018; a null interaction would support the current view that feature_018 is a relatively specific modifier of the feature_063/feature_038 interaction.\n\nThe final four proposals add a bounded broad exploration of an untested standardized numeric predictor, feature_044, as a possible modifier of the dominant clean tag effects. They test clean feature_010, feature_002, feature_027, and feature_037 effects in settings where the other dominant tags are absent, and ask whether high feature_044 makes those contrasts more negative. For positive tags, a negative interaction represents attenuation; for negative tags, a negative interaction represents amplification. This is not intended as a primary discovery channel, but it is a useful specificity screen: if feature_044 modifies dominant clean tags, the compact model of four dominant binary tags plus a feature_063 context model is incomplete. If all are near null, the dominant-tag model remains the simplest dataset-specific description.\n\nTogether, these proposals target the two unresolved scientific questions that remain most informative: whether the clean feature_038 gate survives high feature_018, and whether feature_018's modifier role and the dominant-tag structure are specific rather than broadly replaceable by other continuous predictors. Sparse cells, near-threshold lower bounds, wrong-direction estimates, or intervals crossing threshold will be treated cautiously as unresolved or unsupported, not as definitive evidence of absence."
