  "narrative": "No assessments are due and no independent validation request is available. I register clinically oriented feature_051 stratum follow-ups, treating feature_051 as the most plausible natural-log progression-free-survival proxy, using broad thresholds feature_051 >= 2.70 for higher log PFS and feature_051 <= 2.65 for lower log PFS. For the accepted clean feature_063 high-feature_038 gate, the falsifiable expectation is that a negative feature_063 association remains threshold-supported within both higher and lower log-PFS strata; a separate positive interaction claim tests whether higher log PFS attenuates, rather than amplifies, the gated negative contrast. For the dominant clean tags, the expectation is persistence of the large positive feature_010 and feature_002 associations and the large negative feature_027 and feature_037 associations within both log-PFS strata. A threshold-supported stratum-specific failure or a strong interaction would indicate clinical-PFS heterogeneity or incompleteness of the current dominant-tag plus feature_063 context model; all-stratum persistence would strengthen the dataset-specific robustness of that model. These proposals use feature_051 through eligibility or subgroup conditions rather than as an exact-valued continuous exposure, reducing sparse-cell risk. All new claims are registered as unresolved; returned signed estimates and intervals will be interpreted directly against the 0.15 absolute composite dependency-score-unit threshold. Conclusions remain dataset-specific associations only and not causal, biological, clinical, mechanistic, or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis ledger notes. Threshold = 0.15 absolute composite dependency-score units. No independent validation quota remains. All conclusions are dataset-specific associations only, not causal, biological, clinical, mechanistic, or generalizable claims. Dominant robust tags: feature_010 positive (R23 and many strata); feature_002 positive (R46, validated R52); feature_027 negative (R113, validated R118); feature_037 negative (R62, clean R66 validated R78). Broad modifier tests of feature_018 and feature_038 as modifiers of dominant tags are largely null, as are feature_044 dominant-tag specificity tests. feature_063 context model: marginal feature_063 is not robustly negative because lower bounds fall below threshold, but clean contexts support negative associations; high feature_038 gates a large negative feature_063 contrast, high feature_018 attenuates but does not abolish it, low feature_038 does not support a negative feature_063 contrast, and feature_036/feature_044 are not supported feature_063 modifiers. feature_007, feature_058, feature_015 are not meaningful in tested contrasts. Many other binary/categorical predictors are null, below threshold, wrong direction, or underpowered; feature_019 remains unresolved because informative cells are small or missing. New pending feature_051 candidate log-PFS screen: registered broad higher/lower strata using feature_051 >= 2.70 and feature_051 <= 2.65, with clean feature_063 high-feature_038 gate tests plus a higher-log-PFS attenuation interaction, and clean dominant-tag tests for feature_010, feature_002, feature_027, and feature_037 within each log-PFS stratum. If all dominant clean tag tests and feature_063 gate tests remain threshold-supported across strata, feature_051 is likely not a major modifier of the accepted model in this dataset. If a stratum fails despite adequate cells or the feature_051 interaction is threshold-supported, expand the context model to include clinical progression-survival heterogeneity. Interpret signed estimates directly against the threshold and treat small exposed cells as caution, not proof of absence."
