  "research_notes": "Final dataset-specific model. Dominant accepted binary tags: feature_010=1 positive association (R23 and many strata), feature_002=1 positive association (R46, validated R52), feature_027=1 negative association (R113, validated R118), feature_037=1 negative association (R62, clean R66/R74, validated R78). feature_063 is not robustly marginal but is negative in clean contexts (R128, validated R131; R192) and much stronger under feature_038 >=0 (R149/R150, interaction R157; clean gate R158/R169/R193/R210/R214; feature_051 strata R253/R254). feature_018 attenuates but does not abolish high-feature_038 feature_063 gate (R233/R234 and related accepted interactions). feature_019 standalone remains unresolved/sparse (R8/R13/R255), though the gated feature_063 effect remains accepted under partial feature_019 stratification (R256/R257). feature_036, feature_044, feature_051 broad, feature_007/058/015 markers, and most other predictors do not show supported meaningful effects, though some small-cell interactions remain unresolved or imprecise (R183/R190/R236/R258 etc.).\n\nFinal explore plan: registered nine clean joint-tag mean-difference refinements to test additivity and context dependence among dominant tags. Positive-tag effects are tested when another positive tag, feature_037, or feature_063 is present, while negative tags and feature_063 are excluded where possible. Negative feature_037 effect is tested when feature_010 or feature_002 is present and feature_027/feature_063 are excluded. Parent links attach these to broader earlier accepted tag-specific contrasts. Interpret signed estimates against 0.15 absolute composite dependency-score units. Sparse invalid cells or lower bounds crossing threshold remain unresolved. No further validation requests are available; all conclusions remain dataset-specific associations only."
